  "summary": "Read from Vultr's own open plans endpoint, api.vultr.com/v2/plans-metal, which anyone can open without a key and which each row links beside the provider name; the name leads to Vultr's pricing page, which answers our reader 403 but opens in a browser. Each plan there is priced twice, on demand and preemptible, and says of each price whether it can be deployed that way; only a price it says you can deploy is shown here. Prices are for the whole machine, divided by its number of GPUs. Plans that sell a fraction of a GPU are not listed.",
  "notes": "bare-metal plans endpoint /v2/plans-metal (keyless); a rate is published only where the endpoint says the plan can be deployed that way (deploy_ondemand, deploy_preemptible), so eight plans that state an hourly_cost while saying deploy_ondemand:false are not published as on-demand rates; preemptible recorded as spot, and skipped when equal to the plan's own on-demand price (the same figure twice); the fractional cloud GPU plans in /v2/plans are not read",
